    - The press reader (g4Press2024, ASK 357): a line that says the answer does not meet the PRESS leaves the pressed witness unanswered (ruling 372), so it takes the unanswered-witness path and an honest retraction of it cures. It reads the whole line outside quotations, not only from GROUND on. P1: "answer misses / does not meet / did not meet / fails to meet / does not answer the <up to 3 words> press" or "pressed". P2: "press" or "pressed", up to 2 words, then "is not met" or "was not met". Not read: for P1, a meaning word (meaning, sense or reading, singular or plural) in the words between "the" and "press", or directly or one word after "press" or "pressed"; for P2, a meaning word in the words between "press" or "pressed" and "is/was not met", or anywhere earlier in the clause; for either, a clause that ends in a meaning word just before the match, or that holds not, never, no or nor before the match. So "the answer misses the meaning pressed", "the pressed meaning is not met" and "the meaning that was pressed is not met" stay meaning breaks.
